course: dictionary
lesson: 15856
title: Unfastened and unfasten
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unfastened means not fastened: not closed, not done up, not tied. You can work it out from its parts. The start un- means not, and fastened means closed or joined tight. «The gate was unfastened, so the dog ran out.» The gate was not closed, so it swung open.
explain: Unfasten is the verb, and it means to open or undo something. «Unfasten the buckle» tells you to undo it. «Can you unfasten the clasp on my necklace?» asks you to do the same action.
explain: Safety matters with this word. «His seat belt was unfastened on the bus.» That means it was not done up, so it could not keep him safe if the bus stopped suddenly. Always check that your seat belt and helmet strap are fastened before you move.
fact: Unfastened means not fastened, not closed or done up.
fact: Unfasten means to open or undo something, such as a buckle, clasp or button.
fact: The un- at the start means not, so unfastened is the opposite of fastened.
fact: «Unfastened» can describe a seat belt, a coat, a gate or shoelaces.
fact: An unfastened seat belt or helmet strap is dangerous, so always check it is done up.
exercise: «The coat was unfastened, so the cold wind got in.» What does unfastened mean here? | *Not done up, so it was open at the front | Very warm and thick | Wet through from the rain | Not done up
exercise: «Please unfasten the clasp on the bag.» What does unfasten mean? | To paint | *To open or undo | To fasten tightly | To lose
exercise: What does «came unfastened» mean? | Came apart in pieces | Came closed very tightly | *Came undone and was no longer closed | Came back again
test: «Dad checked that his seat belt was not unfastened before the car moved.» What does unfastened mean in this sentence? | Broken into pieces | *Not done up | Made of metal | Done up very tightly
test: Which word means to open or undo a button? | Fasten | Fastening | Fastened | *Unfasten
exam: Before the bus moves, the driver says, «Check your seat belt is not unfastened.» What does she want you to do? | *Check it is done up | Unfasten it and sit back | Take it off | Leave it loose so it is comfortable
